  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nMarkets are opening higher across the board with SPY at $748.17 (+0.79%) as Iran tensions dominate the tape. VIX dropping 2.54% to 27.65 suggests traders are buying the geopolitical dip, but oil spiking 3% is keeping risk assets on edge.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NY Empire State Manufacturing (12:30 ET)</strong> - First major data drop of the day, watch for any signs of industrial weakness from Iran war impacts</li>\n<li><strong>Industrial Production (1:15 ET)</strong> - Multiple manufacturing metrics hitting at once, could move the needle on economic growth narrative</li>\n<li><strong>Oil Rig Count (5:00 ET)</strong> - With crude up 3% on Iran news, this could extend energy's momentum into next week</li>\n<li><strong>Trump-Iran Headlines</strong> - President says decision on Chinese sanctions coming soon, any escalation will hit markets hard</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Iran crisis is the main event. Trump's patience wearing thin while airlines cancel flights and Germany braces for economic hit. Oil spike is real.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nTech leading the charge at +1.50% (XLK) while defensive plays like Real Estate (-0.68%) and Materials (-0.75%) are getting sold. Energy up 0.76% on oil surge, but it's tech carrying the load again. Classic risk-on rotation despite geopolitical noise.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>VIX falling while markets rise suggests institutional buying. Tech leadership with falling volatility is a powerful combo for momentum.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Oil at 3% gains will hit margins across the board. If Iran situation escalates, this market optimism will reverse fast and hard.</div>\n